From: Llaminar native capture retirement regression
Subject: [PATCH] Retire fork membership before recursive EndCapture descent

Auxiliary-stream reentry can form cyclic parallel stream membership while
the captured event/node graph remains acyclic. Detach children and reset
local capture bookkeeping before recursion, so repeated visits terminate without
removing any graph dependency, changing native execution or retaining a ledger.
The caller's preserveInvalidated value propagates unchanged to every visit.

Pinned base: ROCm/rocm-systems 7da43026e4f2ef7600433c38c820732f7a205d22
             (therock-10.1, ROCm Core SDK 10.1.0)

--- a/hipamd/src/hip_stream.cpp
+++ b/hipamd/src/hip_stream.cpp
@@ -62,21 +62,26 @@
     }
     captureEvents_.clear();
   }
-  // Recursively end capture on all parallel (forked) streams.
-  for (auto stream : parallelCaptureStreams_) {
-    [[maybe_unused]] const auto err =
-        reinterpret_cast<hip::Stream*>(stream)->EndCapture(preserveInvalidated);
-    assert(err == hipSuccess);
-  }
-
-  // Reset all capture state to defaults.
+  // Fork/rejoin event dependencies are acyclic in time, but stream membership
+  // may revisit an earlier stream. Detach that membership before descending:
+  // an already visited stream then has no children to follow a second time.
+  // This changes cleanup ownership only, never the captured node/event DAG.
+  auto parallel_capture_streams = std::move(parallelCaptureStreams_);
+  parallelCaptureStreams_.clear();
+
+  // Reset this stream before recursion so cyclic and diamond membership is
+  // idempotent. Preserve invalidation exactly as the original caller requests.
   captureStatus_ = preserveInvalidated ? hipStreamCaptureStatusInvalidated
                                        : hipStreamCaptureStatusNone;
   pCaptureGraph_ = nullptr;
   originStream_ = false;
   parentStream_ = nullptr;
   lastCapturedNodes_.clear();
-  parallelCaptureStreams_.clear();
+  for (auto stream : parallel_capture_streams) {
+    [[maybe_unused]] const auto err =
+        reinterpret_cast<hip::Stream*>(stream)->EndCapture(preserveInvalidated);
+    assert(err == hipSuccess);
+  }
 
   return hipSuccess;
 }
